  "id": "dead-blocks",
  "name": "The Dead Blocks",
  "description": "The edge of Old Town where the reconstructed blocks stop and the dead blocks begin. On the left, the back of a re-clad apartment block, warm windows behind blinds and a steel service door under a caged bulb. A tall boundary wall runs across, broken through in the middle and hung with a sheet of corrugated metal. Beyond it a condemned hab tower, bricked-up and boarded windows, washing on a line, one lantern high up, an open stairwell with a lit hand lantern, and at its foot a drum fire with a few plastic chairs. Cracked asphalt, weeds and rubble in front; the city's towers far off between the buildings.",
